  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758515,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## $100,000 Pyramid, The (Commodore 64) - Game Description\n\nStep into the fast-paced world of the classic TV game show with *$100,000 Pyramid, The* for the Commodore 64! This early adaptation brings the excitement of the pyramid-climbing challenge directly to your living room. The goal is simple: reach the peak of the pyramid by correctly guessing words based on your partner's clever clues.\n\nEach round presents a category – think \"things that are red\" or \"types of vehicles\" – filled with hidden words. One player acts as the clue-giver, desperately trying to convey the words without uttering them directly. Quick thinking and sharp deduction are key to success!  A single-player mode offers a different, less traditional experience, tasking you with providing single-word clues to a computer opponent.\n\nExperience the thrill of rapid-fire guessing and strategic clue-giving as you race against the clock.  With its simple yet addictive gameplay and faithful recreation of the TV show's core mechanics, *$100,000 Pyramid, The* delivers a fun and engaging experience for players of all ages. Can you conquer the pyramid and"
    },
